+ * APU's frame thread, trying once a frame, went 80 ms and more without one
+ * (and the OHCI and DPC claims here run out their hold-offs and go ahead
+ * anyway, beside the guest). On the console an interrupt is taken at the
+ * next instruction. The nearest thing here: while a caller waits, a thread
+ * about to raise steps aside (irql_count_raise), so the wait is only for the
+ * sections already running, which are microseconds.
+ *
+ * Returns 1 with the processor claimed, or 0 with nothing claimed after
+ * max_ms, or after 1 ms in which no thread crossed the boundary: a depth that
+ * does not move is a raise that leaked or a section that will not end soon,
+ * and holding every other raise back behind it would stall the title. The
+ * caller must hold no lock a raised thread could want. */
+int xbox_IrqlClaimProcessorWait(int max_ms)
+{
